      "explanation": "trtllm_dev.sh creates the dev container without CAP_SYS_PTRACE, so every test that starts an MPI pool dies inside mpi4py's pidfd_getfd. It is a property of the container and no DeepSeek-V4 change can cause or fix it from inside the repository.",
      "id": "container_lacks_cap_sys_ptrace"
    },
    {
      "all_of": [
        "torch.OutOfMemoryError",
        "CUDA out of memory"
      ],
      "explanation": "DEEPSEEK_V4_TINY_CONFIG is only tiny in depth: 7 layers of 256 unquantized BF16 routed experts at hidden 4096 / intermediate 2048 need more than the 79.18 GiB this H100 has, and the construction dies after allocating 75.34 GiB. The test's ModelConfig is built directly rather than through from_pretrained, so the checkpoint's quantization_config never applies and the experts stay BF16. iteration 31 pristine probe: the DeepSeek-V4 production diff was stashed, leaving the tree at fe4aebfe0f, and this test failed there with the same message; the working tree was then restored byte-identically (git diff sha256 e7b554b77ac53df24b6106b050637cd6877dada61124f0ba6879d57a9e66a5f5 before and after). Log: /cache/dsv4_flash_h100/iter31/pristine_two.log",
      "id": "model_exceeds_this_nodes_80gb_hbm"
    },
